---
import { buyerRepresentationPage } from '../data/buyer-representation';
import ServiceLayout from '../layouts/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { createServiceSchema } from '../utils/seo';

const serviceSchema = createServiceSchema({
  name: 'Yacht Buyer Representation',
  serviceType: 'Yacht buyer representation and technical purchase support',
  pathname: buyerRepresentationPage.pathname,
  description: buyerRepresentationPage.schemaDescription,
  areaServed: buyerRepresentationPage.areaServed,
});
---

<ServiceLayout
  title={buyerRepresentationPage.title}
  description={buyerRepresentationPage.description}
  locale="en"
  routeId="buyerRepresentation"
  pathname={buyerRepresentationPage.pathname}
  heading={buyerRepresentationPage.heading}
  eyebrow={buyerRepresentationPage.eyebrow}
  summary={buyerRepresentationPage.summary}
  heroImage={buyerRepresentationPage.heroImage}
  socialImageAlt={buyerRepresentationPage.heroImage.alt}
  breadcrumbs={buyerRepresentationPage.breadcrumbs}
  primaryCta={buyerRepresentationPage.primaryCta}
  secondaryCta={buyerRepresentationPage.secondaryCta}
  relatedServices={buyerRepresentationPage.relatedServices}
  finalCta={buyerRepresentationPage.finalCta}
  structuredData={serviceSchema}
>
  <section aria-labelledby="independent-support-heading">
    <h2 id="independent-support-heading">
      Independent Support for Yacht Buyers
    </h2>
    <p>
      Buying a yacht can involve technical, financial and practical decisions
      that are difficult to evaluate from sales information alone.
    </p>
    <p>
      All Yacht Service provides independent technical support for buyers
      before, during and after the purchase of sailing yachts, motor yachts and
      catamarans.
    </p>
    <p>
      The service is particularly valuable for international buyers purchasing
      yachts in Spain or elsewhere in the Mediterranean, as well as buyers who
      cannot personally attend every viewing, inspection, sea trial or
      repair-yard appointment.
    </p>
    <p>
      Support is provided by Aleksandrs Tolkacovs, an IIMS-Certified Yacht and
      Small Craft Marine Surveyor and licensed captain, with more than 20 years
      of experience in engineering, quality assurance and management.
    </p>
    <p class="service-note">
      The exact scope is agreed individually according to the yacht, location,
      purchase stage and level of support required.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="buyer-types-heading">
    <h2 id="buyer-types-heading">Who Can Benefit from Buyer Representation?</h2>
    <p>Yacht buyer representation may be useful when:</p>
    <div class="inspection-grid">
      {
        buyerRepresentationPage.buyerTypes.map((item) => (
          <article>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.description}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="service-note">
      The service provides technical and practical support. It does not
      guarantee that a suitable yacht will be found or purchased.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="service-scope-heading">
    <h2 id="service-scope-heading">
      What Yacht Buyer Representation Can Include
    </h2>
    <p>
      The service can be adapted to the stage of the purchase and the buyer’s
      requirements. Depending on the agreed scope, support may include:
    </p>
    <div class="inspection-grid">
      {
        buyerRepresentationPage.serviceItems.map((item) => (
          <article>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p>{item.description}</p>
          </article>
        ))
      }
    </div>
    <p class="service-note">
      Services are limited to the agreed technical and practical scope. Legal,
      tax, financial, registration and contractual matters should be reviewed by
      appropriately qualified professional advisers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="before-offer-heading">
    <h2 id="before-offer-heading">Technical Support Before Making an Offer</h2>
    <p>
      Before making an offer, a buyer may want an initial understanding of the
      yacht’s apparent condition and major technical risks.
    </p>
    <p>
      A pre-offer technical inspection can help identify obvious concerns before
      the buyer commits to the time and cost of a comprehensive survey.
    </p>
    <p>Depending on the agreed scope, this may include:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {buyerRepresentationPage.preOfferItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="service-note">
      A pre-offer inspection is limited in scope and does not replace a
      {' '}
      <a class="text-link" href="/pre-purchase-survey"
        >comprehensive pre-purchase yacht survey</a
      >.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="survey-purchase-heading">
    <h2 id="survey-purchase-heading">
      Support During the Survey and Purchase Process
    </h2>
    <p>
      A full survey can produce a substantial amount of technical information.
      Buyer representation helps the client understand which findings are most
      significant and how they may affect safety, maintenance, repair planning
      and the decision to proceed.
    </p>
    <p>Support may include:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {
        buyerRepresentationPage.surveySupportItems.map((item) => (
          <li>{item}</li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="service-note">
      All commercial decisions remain with the buyer. All Yacht Service does not
      guarantee the outcome of negotiations or the completion of the purchase.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="negotiation-support-heading">
    <h2 id="negotiation-support-heading">
      Using Survey Findings During Negotiations
    </h2>
    <p>
      Survey findings may provide the buyer with a clearer basis for discussing
      repairs, completion conditions or the purchase price.
    </p>
    <p>
      All Yacht Service can explain the technical significance and likely
      priority of identified defects so the buyer can make informed decisions
      and communicate more effectively with the seller or broker.
    </p>
    <p>Where requested and appropriate, support may include:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {buyerRepresentationPage.negotiationItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="service-note">
      The service provides technical information and practical support. It does
      not provide legal advice, contractual representation or any guarantee that
      the seller will agree to repairs, discounts or other requested terms.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="after-purchase-heading">
    <h2 id="after-purchase-heading">Technical Support After the Purchase</h2>
    <p>Support can continue after the purchase is completed.</p>
    <p>Depending on the buyer’s requirements, this may include:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {buyerRepresentationPage.postPurchaseItems.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
      <li>
        <a class="text-link" href="/yacht-delivery"
          >Professional yacht delivery</a
        > to the new marina or destination
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p class="service-note">
      All Yacht Service can coordinate agreed work and technical specialists but
      does not imply that it directly performs every repair or specialist
      technical task.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="international-buyers-heading">
    <h2 id="international-buyers-heading">
      Support for International Yacht Buyers
    </h2>
    <p>
      Purchasing a yacht in another country can create additional challenges,
      including travel, language, marina access, local contractors,
      documentation and coordination between several parties.
    </p>
    <p>
      Based at Marina Greenwich in Altea, All Yacht Service can act as the
      buyer’s independent technical contact in Spain and other Mediterranean
      locations.
    </p>
    <p>The service may help international buyers:</p>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {
        buyerRepresentationPage.internationalBuyerItems.map((item) => (
          <li>{item}</li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>
    <p class="service-note">
      Legal ownership, registration, tax, customs and contractual matters remain
      the responsibility of the buyer and their appropriately qualified
      professional advisers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="independence-heading">
    <h2 id="independence-heading">
      Independent Advice and Conflict Disclosure
    </h2>
    <p>
      Buyer representation is intended to provide clear technical information in
      the interests of the commissioning client.
    </p>
    <p>
      Any commercial relationship or potential conflict of interest connected
      with a vessel will be disclosed before an appointment is accepted.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a conflict could prevent an independent service from being provided,
      the assignment may be declined or its limitations agreed clearly with the
      client.
    </p>
    <p class="service-note">
      All Yacht Service does not receive authority to make the final purchase
      decision on behalf of the client unless a separate and legally appropriate
      written arrangement has been established.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="brokerage-heading">
    <h2 id="brokerage-heading">Buyer Representation and Yacht Brokerage</h2>
    <p>
      A yacht broker normally assists with marketing, introducing buyers and
      sellers, arranging viewings and progressing the commercial transaction.
    </p>
    <p>
      Yacht buyer representation from All Yacht Service focuses on independent
      technical support, vessel condition, survey findings, repair priorities
      and practical purchase decisions.
    </p>
    <p>
      The service does not replace the buyer’s legal adviser, tax adviser,
      registration specialist or other appropriately qualified professional.
    </p>
    <p>
      Where a yacht has a commercial connection with All Yacht Service, Premium
      Yachts Spain or another associated party, that relationship will be
      disclosed before the assignment is accepted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="buyer-process-heading">
    <h2 id="buyer-process-heading">How Yacht Buyer Representation Works</h2>
    <ol class="process-list">
      {
        buyerRepresentationPage.processSteps.map((step, index) => (
          <li>
            <div>
              <span aria-hidden="true">
                {String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}
              </span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <h3>{step.title}</h3>
              <p>{step.description}</p>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="coverage-heading">
    <h2 id="coverage-heading">
      Yacht Buyer Representation Across Spain and the Mediterranean
    </h2>
    <p>
      Based at Marina Greenwich in Altea, All Yacht Service provides yacht buyer
      representation and technical purchase support throughout Alicante, Costa
      Blanca, Valencia, Barcelona, the Spanish Mediterranean coast and other
      locations across mainland Spain.
    </p>
    <p>
      Support in the Balearic Islands, France, Italy, Greece and other European
      or international locations can also be arranged according to the yacht’s
      location and the required scope.
    </p>
    <p>
      Remote document review and technical consultation may also be available
      where an immediate physical inspection is not required.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section aria-labelledby="why-buyer-representation-heading">
    <h2 id="why-buyer-representation-heading">Why Choose All Yacht Service?</h2>
    <ul class="service-check-list">
      {buyerRepresentationPage.whyChoose.map((item) => <li>{item}</li>)}
    </ul>
  </section>
</ServiceLayout>
